{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>It will be filled before its day</b> — Most of the commentators said: that the alef is in place of a doubled lamed, and it is from וקטפת מלילות, and in the language of our Rabbis: מוללו ומריח בו." "<b>And it will be gathered</b> — From כפה ואגמון."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The verse phrase תמלא is discussed with an alef functioning as a doubled lamed; the rabbinic citation appears to reference a halakhic context about checking produce."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:46.343268704Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}